 an altar be mobile? if your haven is an RV, or Yacht?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I would be fine with it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-25T14:36:35-07:00","id":1222111,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1060847-cruac-show-me-some-rituals-that-benefit-from-altars?p=1221991#post1221991\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would say no. An altar is a table or platform for offering sacrifices or preparing consecrated items. They would be profaning it by carrying it around and stashing it in a dirty or high traffic area or having it double as a coffee table. Now if they want to set it up and conduct appropriate purification rituals in an RV or boat just prior to use that\u2019s another thing.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> How long would setting it up and &quot;appropropriate purification ritual's take?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-25T17:41:49-07:00","id":1222134,"title":"","content":"However long it would take to clean the area where it would be set up and make appropriate prayers for purification and sanctification.<br /> <br /> The cult I was part of once would spend at least an hour each week cleaning up the semi private room and praying for God's presence where speaking in tongues and translating would take place. They'd spend hours dredging the pond prior to conducting full immersion baptisms.<br /> <br /> The Shinto Buddhist I work with arrives about 15 minutes before his shift starts at least three times a week, cleaning, praying, and rearranging the shrine at his desk and making sure the other books, papers, and objects on his desk are aligned properly. And every night before he leaves he spends at least 5 minutes rearranging his desk as well. I know he takes it seriously because he can often tell if someone has taken something and replaced it later from his shelves after he left for the night.<br /> <br /> To me that comes down more to individual character flavor. If a player isn't going to bother with describing how their character keeps their altar consecrated and playing it out when appropriate, they aren't going to get the bonuses for it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5466,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","user":"tsusasi","date":". 08-07-2018, 11:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-25T18:14:15-07:00","id":1222138,"title":"","content":"I practice shinto myself, I try to go out to the park in the morning and face the sun recite Nippashi off my E reader and bow low to the sun.<br /> <br /> With a recent heat wave I cant risk being out in the heat<br /> <br /> Showing the truth in one book I have on Shinto that why Amateratsu may be benevolent her order can become oppressive and this is why we need Susano.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"